[Unit]
Description=Run the NSE rebalance scan daily at 15:00 (weekdays, ~30min before market close -- also refreshes the Screener page's cache). Deliberately NOT pre-market: Kite's historical "day" candle for today updates live intraday, so running close to the close gives the ranking/sizing pipeline a same-day price basis matching backtest.py's own same-day-close assumption, instead of pre-market's stale prior-day close (which also risked a gap-up open invalidating the day's sizing). The observed run time is ~13 minutes (see the Job Log page's rebalance_scan duration), leaving ~17min of margin before 15:30 close -- re-check that duration history before ever moving this later; it must finish with enough margin before 15:30 close for auto_execute_trades (if enabled) to place valid regular-hours orders.

[Timer]
OnCalendar=Mon..Fri 15:00
Persistent=false
Unit=nse-rebalance.service

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
